# OCR Service Test Data - Typed Documents Quality Variations .gitignore
#
# This file specifies which document files should be excluded from version control
# to prevent repository bloat while ensuring that documentation and configuration
# files are properly tracked.
#
# The quality_variations directory contains test documents with varying quality levels
# (high, medium, low) to test the OCR service's robustness against different document qualities.

# Exclude all binary document files by default
*.pdf
*.PDF
*.tiff
*.TIFF
*.tif
*.TIF
*.png
*.PNG
*.jpg
*.JPG
*.jpeg
*.JPEG

# Exclude large data files
*.zip
*.ZIP
*.tar.gz
*.TAR.GZ

# Exclude temporary files
*.tmp
*~

# Keep all README files and documentation
!README.md
!README.txt
!*.md

# Keep configuration files
!*.json
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.config

# Keep metadata files
!metadata.csv
!document_index.csv
!annotations.csv
!quality_metrics.csv

# INSTRUCTIONS FOR TEST DOCUMENTS
#
# The actual test documents are not stored in the Git repository to avoid bloat.
# To obtain the quality variation test documents for development and testing:
#
# 1. Download the quality variation test document package from the secure S3 bucket:
#    s3://mca-documents-staging/test-data/typed_documents/quality_variations.zip
#
# 2. Extract the package to this directory, preserving the folder structure
#
# 3. Run the verification script to ensure all required test documents are present:
#    python ../../../verify_test_data.py typed_documents/quality_variations
#
# 4. The quality_variations directory contains documents with the following quality levels:
#    - high_quality/: Documents with clear text and optimal scanning conditions
#    - medium_quality/: Documents with moderate noise, slight blurring, or lower resolution
#    - low_quality/: Documents with significant noise, blurring, or poor scanning conditions
#
# For more information, see the README.md file in this directory.